/tools/
/.metadata/
/.vscode/

# ── STM32CubeIDE build output ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Everything under a session's Debug/ or Release/ is compiler output: .o,
# .d, .su, .cyclo, the generated .mk files and makefile, the .elf/.map and
# the .bin. Verified before untracking that these directories contain no
# hand-written .c, .h, .ld, .ioc or .cproject — the linker script lives one
# level up in STM32CubeIDE/FSBL/ and stays tracked.
#
# Untracking does not delete anything: the files stay on disk, the IDE keeps
# writing there, and building and flashing are unchanged. A fresh clone needs
# one build before it can flash, which the IDE handles by regenerating the
# makefiles from .cproject.
#
# This stops FUTURE growth only. Sessions 06-16's build output is already in
# history and stays there; shrinking that would mean rewriting history, which
# is not worth doing to a submission repo.
# Sessions 01-05 predate the STM32CubeIDE/ layout and put Debug/ elsewhere,
# so the pattern is rooted at sessions/ rather than at a fixed depth.
sessions/**/Debug/
sessions/**/Release/
